# Token thrift

When this chat already has an approved design, or the user says «ok», «procedi», «implementa come approvato», «commit», or «PR»:

- Do **not** re-read Superpowers skills, wiki `INDEX.md`, graphify, or claude-mem.
- Do **not** brainstorm alternatives. Implement, or git/PR if they asked that.
- Orientation (`CLAUDE.md`, wiki) only if the task is new and ambiguous.
- Do **not** write `docs/superpowers/specs/` or `plans/` unless the user explicitly asks.

Still apply: Italian player copy, TDD for new logic, one concern per PR, lint/test/build before opening a PR, no commit unless asked. PR/issue English: skill **`no-ai-slop`**. Never `Co-authored-by: Cursor`.
